// D1602 — a CLOSURE value delivered at every position under a name a module function also
// carries, then CALLED through it. The prelude's `function v(): i32` is what makes each
// function-scoped cell a shadow; the emitter's call arm resolved the callee by name before
// asking the scope, so `v(8)` lowered to a direct `call` on that function.
//
// The module-scope positions are skipped for the reason the `global-shadowed-by-local`
// template gives: a second top-level `v` beside the prelude's declaration is `redeclared v`,
// not a shadow, so those cells would grade the duplicate rule rather than this capability.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@PRELUDE@@
function v(): i32 { 6 }
// @@VALUE@@
(n: i32) => { print(n) }
// @@TYPE@@
(i32) => void
// @@PROOF@@
v(8)
// @@WANT@@
8
// @@SKIP@@
binding: a second module-scope `v` is `redeclared v`, not a shadow
return_inferred: the receiving binding is module-scope — `redeclared v`
return_annotated: the receiving binding is module-scope — `redeclared v`
struct_field_init: the destination binding is module-scope — `redeclared v`
struct_field_assign: the rebind is module-scope — `redeclared v`
array_element: the list binding is module-scope — `redeclared v`
array_element_assign: the rebind is module-scope — `redeclared v`
array_push: the rebind is module-scope — `redeclared v`
global_init: a global named `v` beside the prelude's is `redeclared v`
global_assign: a global named `v` beside the prelude's is `redeclared v`
two_instances: both bindings are module-scope — `redeclared v`
map_value: a closure read out of a map and bound is check-clean invalid wasm with no shadow in sight — the cell grades that, not this
block_if_capture: a lambda in a module-scope block, over a closure it captured from that block, refuses `call to unknown function` with no shadow in sight
block_while_capture: same as `block_if_capture` — the captured-closure gap, not a shadow
block_bare_capture: same as `block_if_capture` — the captured-closure gap, not a shadow
